WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:06.620
Here's a week of lead follow-up at a made-up plumbing company. Every message you'll see is the real output of the code.

2
00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:13.940
Monday morning, Maria fills in the website form. Her name is in capitals, and her email has a typo.

3
00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:18.310
The owner gets her details straight away, phone number included.

4
00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:24.430
And Maria gets a reply in seconds, with the typo fixed, so she knows she's been heard.

5
00:00:27.830 --> 00:00:32.490
She writes again, but it's still one conversation. No second auto-reply.

6
00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:42.500
That evening, Wei asks for a quote, and he's answered instantly too.

7
00:00:45.900 --> 00:00:51.390
Bob left no usable email or phone, so instead of guessing, it goes straight to the owner.

8
00:00:52.440 --> 00:00:56.440
Maria hasn't replied by Tuesday, so she gets one friendly follow-up.

9
00:00:57.490 --> 00:00:59.790
She answers, and her follow-ups stop.

10
00:01:00.840 --> 00:01:04.810
Wei's follow-up fell due at night, so it waited until nine in the morning.

11
00:01:08.210 --> 00:01:14.840
Lead follow-up is four hundred and fifty dollars, fixed, and built in your own accounts. The link is on screen.
